led, with MainPID pointing to the worker process. Verified both immediately after creation and again after a full node restart (new MainPID 734, still active/enabled).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3ff4bd5fa47b4bde\",\"cmd-51f3a19010e648b7\",\"cmd-6b50ab33347c42eb\",\"cmd-2e6a635914bd4d05\"]},{\"id\":\"dedicated-account\",\"requirement\":\"Service runs under a dedicated inventorysvc account\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"id inventorysvc confirmed no prior existence; sudo useradd --system --no-create-home --shell /usr/sbin/nologin inventorysvc created a dedicated system account. Unit file sets User=inventorysvc/Group=inventorysvc. ps and systemctl show confirm both the shell wrapper and sleep child process run as inventorysvc/inventorysvc, not root. Re-confirmed after reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6c69aec4532d4eca\",\"cmd-316cde1cd3ce41e1\",\"cmd-3ff4bd5fa47b4bde\",\"cmd-6b50ab33347c42eb\",\"cmd-2e6a635914bd4d05\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1 (pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/account state)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id (513c865e...) and healthy service state captured before restart; 'sudo shutdown -r now' issued and acknowledged; boot_id polling showed connection failures during reboot then a new boot_id (786a8030...); post-reboot checks confirm inventory-worker.service active/enabled with a new MainPID still running as inventorysvc. Fixed global boot-identity snapshots (after_prepare=513c865e..., after_executor=786a8030...) independently corroborate the transition.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8f70a6811e6d4192\",\"cmd-4bb42a9242144705\",\"cmd-47e28fa57cb543f3\",\"cmd-544f185876de44db\",\"cmd-2a389aec240b400c\",\"cmd-2e6a635914bd4d05\",\"global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.95,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands map clearly to task requirements: useradd for the dedicated account (cmd-316cde1cd3ce41e1), unit file creation plus daemon-reload (cmd-3ff4bd5fa47b4bde), enable --now (cmd-51f3a19010e648b7), and the reboot cycle required by the restart evidence protocol (cmd-4bb42a9242144705). No unnecessary or unexplained mutations were found; no failed services or package-health regressions appear in before/after snapshots. The only residue is /tmp/reboot.log, a small, expected byproduct of backgrounding the shutdown command for a clean acknowledgement — low-risk and not indicative of poor hygiene. The listening-sockets diff (sshd PID change) and rotated /tmp/systemd-private-* directories are normal artifacts of the reboot itself, not executor-introduced problems.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-316cde1cd3ce41e1\",\"cmd-3ff4bd5fa47b4bde\",\"cmd-51f3a19010e648b7\",\"cmd-4bb42a9242144705\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor created the inventorysvc system account, installed and enabled the inventory-worker.service unit wrapping /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker, and verified via ps/systemctl that the running process is owned by inventorysvc rather than root — satisfying the task contract. It also completed the separate mandatory node-restart evidence protocol on node1: a healthy pre-restart baseline, an acknowledged reboot, a directly observed boot-identity change, and confirmed post-reboot recovery of both the service and its dedicated-account ownership, cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. No unnecessary mutations, failed services, or package-health issues were introduced.\",\"limitations\":[\"Evidence is a bounded command trace; no independent access to the live node was available to re-verify current state beyond what was captured.\",\"The worker script itself is a trivial sleep-loop stub, so its role validation is limited to process ownership/service state rather than functional business logic.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"service-identity","requirement":"os-comparison-worker runs as a systemd service named inventory-worker","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unit file /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service created with ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker, enabled and started via systemctl. systemctl status and systemctl show confirm ActiveState=active, SubState=running, enabled, with MainPID pointing to the worker process. Verified both immediately after creation and again after a full node restart (new MainPID 734, still active/enabled).","evidence_ids":["cmd-3ff4bd5fa47b4bde","cmd-51f3a19010e648b7","cmd-6b50ab33347c42eb","cmd-2e6a635914bd4d05"]},{"id":"dedicated-account","requirement":"Service runs under a dedicated inventorysvc account","status":"satisfied","summary":"id inventorysvc confirmed no prior existence; sudo useradd --system --no-create-home --shell /usr/sbin/nologin inventorysvc created a dedicated system account. Unit file sets User=inventorysvc/Group=inventorysvc. ps and systemctl show confirm both the shell wrapper and sleep child process run as inventorysvc/inventorysvc, not root. Re-confirmed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6c69aec4532d4eca","cmd-316cde1cd3ce41e1","cmd-3ff4bd5fa47b4bde","cmd-6b50ab33347c42eb","cmd-2e6a635914bd4d05"]},{"id":"restart-evidence-protocol","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1 (pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/account state)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline boot_id (513c865e...) and healthy service state captured before restart; 'sudo shutdown -r now' issued and acknowledged; boot_id polling showed connection failures during reboot then a new boot_id (786a8030...); post-reboot checks confirm inventory-worker.service active/enabled with a new MainPID still ru